      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T13:52:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried for a long time to get that to work, but couldn\u0027t find a way. toolchain/download_mac_toolchain.bzl, which uses repository_ctx(1) can get both the HOME environment variable as well as the workspace - so it has no problem creating ~/.skiabazel. However, I couldn\u0027t find a way for ctx(2) to access either directory location. If the sole reason for creating MacSDK links in ~/.skiabazel was to put them in an easy to find location, would having a script to display this location suffice? It\u0027s really a no-no to write files outside of the Bazel repository isn\u0027t it?\n\n(1) https://bazel.build/rules/lib/repository_ctx\n(2) https://bazel.build/rules/lib/ctx",
